---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: Which workflows the fix bot reads
    accDescr: A run of a workflow fails. A workflow that the list of after-checks.yml of main doesn't name starts no bot, and the bot reads none of its fixes, whatever a pull request names it. For a workflow of the list, also one of the project's own such as Docker E2E, the bot looks for an artifact fixes-*. Without one, the PR coach explains the check. With one, the bot waits for the workflows whose files on main keep such an artifact, and for no long run that keeps none, up to a quarter of an hour. Then it takes the fixes of every run of the list that failed as data, only text files that the commit has, and commits them as one commit onto a branch of the repository, suggests them on a pull request from a fork, or keeps one pull request with the fixes of main.

    failed(["A run of a workflow fails"])
    listed{"The list of after-checks.yml<br>of main names it?"}
    ignored["No bot starts, and the bot<br>reads none of its fixes"]
    kept{"It kept an artifact<br>fixes-*?"}
    coach["The PR coach explains<br>the check"]
    wait["The bot waits for the workflows whose files on main<br>keep fixes, and for no long run that keeps none"]
    take["It takes the fixes of every run of the list that failed<br>as data, only text files that the commit has"]
    heal["One commit on a branch of the repository, suggestions<br>on a fork, or one pull request for main"]
    list[("workflows: of after-checks.yml<br>CI, Lint, Docker E2E and<br>the answer test_workflows")]

    failed --> listed
    listed -- "no" --> ignored
    listed -- "yes" --> kept
    kept -- "no" --> coach
    kept -- "yes" --> wait --> take --> heal
    list -.-> listed

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class coach,wait,take bot
    class failed person
    class heal done
